From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 14:02:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/v4l2_m2m: set the coded format before the raw one
 when encoding

The V4L2 stateful encoder interface has the client set the coded format
on CAPTURE first, then the raw format on OUTPUT: a driver derives its
raw format from the coded one, and is explicitly allowed to reset
OUTPUT whenever CAPTURE is set. Setting OUTPUT first therefore
negotiates a pixel format that the following CAPTURE S_FMT throws away.

hantro does exactly that. hantro_set_fmt_cap() on an encoder calls
hantro_reset_raw_fmt(), which reinstates the driver's default raw
format, so on the RK3588 VEPU121 JPEG encoder an application that asks
for NM12 ends up with the hardware in YM12 while its own cached
v4l2_format still says NM12. Nothing fails: the encoder reads the
frame's chroma with the wrong plane layout and emits a picture with
corrupt colour.

Set the coded queue first and the raw queue second. Decoding is the
same rule with the queues the other way round, which is the order the
code already used, so nothing changes there.

Signed-off-by: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 libavcodec/v4l2_m2m.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libavcodec/v4l2_m2m.c b/libavcodec/v4l2_m2m.c
index 07c7500000..4dc7116675 100644
--- a/libavcodec/v4l2_m2m.c
+++ b/libavcodec/v4l2_m2m.c
@@ -137,6 +137,7 @@ done:
 static av_cold int v4l2_configure_contexts(V4L2m2mContext *s)
 {
     void *log_ctx = s->avctx;
+    V4L2Context *first, *second;
     int ret;
     struct v4l2_format ofmt, cfmt;
 
@@ -160,15 +161,28 @@ static av_cold int v4l2_configure_contexts(V4L2m2mContext *s)
                                                cfmt.fmt.pix.pixelformat),
                                  av_get_pix_fmt_name(s->capture.av_pix_fmt) ?: "none");
 
-    ret = ff_v4l2_context_set_format(&s->output);
+    /* The queue carrying the coded format goes first. A driver derives the
+     * other queue's format from it and may reset that queue outright when the
+     * coded format is set, so setting them the other way round loses whatever
+     * was negotiated for the raw side. That is CAPTURE when encoding and
+     * OUTPUT when decoding. */
+    if (s->avctx && av_codec_is_encoder(s->avctx->codec)) {
+        first  = &s->capture;
+        second = &s->output;
+    } else {
+        first  = &s->output;
+        second = &s->capture;
+    }
+
+    ret = ff_v4l2_context_set_format(first);
     if (ret) {
-        av_log(log_ctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "can't set v4l2 output format\n");
+        av_log(log_ctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "can't set v4l2 %s format\n", first->name);
         goto error;
     }
 
-    ret = ff_v4l2_context_set_format(&s->capture);
+    ret = ff_v4l2_context_set_format(second);
     if (ret) {
-        av_log(log_ctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "can't to set v4l2 capture format\n");
+        av_log(log_ctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "can't set v4l2 %s format\n", second->name);
         goto error;
     }
 
-- 
